---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="User data">
    <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">User data</h1>

        <p class="mb-4">
            As described <a
                href="/information/sshinfra"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">before</a
            >, all ssh-based games on OverTheWire run in <a
                href="https://www.docker.com/"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">Docker</a
            > containers, which means that the containers are destroyed when you log
            out from SSH.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-4">
            You are free to store data anywhere you like, such as <code
                >/tmp</code
            > or even the home directories. Keep in mind that all of these directories
            will be wiped when you log out, which can get annoying if you just created
            that superfancy exploit and your SSH connection unexpectedly disconnects.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-4">
            That is why we are offering persistent storage on the shell-games.
            To make use of persistent storage, put the following in your SSH
            config:
        </p>

        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-4 mb-6">
            <li>
                Assuming you are using the correct operating system and shell,
                edit your
                <code>~/.bashrc</code> file and add:

                <pre
                    class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded mt-2 overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-gray-300">export OTWUSERDIR="my-overthewire-secret-user-data-directory"</pre>

                <p class="mt-2">
                    You may need to logout and login again for these changes to
                    take effect. To test whether the environment variables are
                    registered, type "echo $OTWUSERDIR", which should show that
                    environment variable.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                Next, edit <code>~/.ssh/config</code> (or create it if it doesn't
                exist) and add:
                <pre
                    class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded mt-2 overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-gray-300">Host *.labs.overthewire.org
  SendEnv OTWUSERDIR</pre>
                <p class="mt-2">
                    This configures your SSH client to transmit the environment
                    variable to your remote session, so it can be used there.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="mb-4">
            Upon the next login to one of the games, your persistent user
            directory will be created. Don't lose the name of the directory,
            because you will not be able to recover it easily. Also, be careful
            about sharing the name of your directory. Anyone with that knowledge
            can read and modify your files in there.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-4">
            Also see the help page about <a
                href="/information/sshinfra"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline"
                >SSH and infrastructure</a
            >.
        </p>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
